source "Kconfig.zephyr"

config ESC_SPI_LOOPBACK_TEST
	bool "Run the SPI loopback self-test instead of talking to the ESC"
	default n
	help
	  Diagnostic build. Clocks a known byte pattern out of MOSI and
	  verifies it arrives back on MISO, which requires those two lines to
	  be physically joined (pull the MOSI and MISO leads off P1 pins 7 and
	  6 and connect them to each other).

	  Use this when every ESC register reads 0xff. A pass proves the ESP32
	  SPI peripheral, the pin mapping and both jumper wires are good, which
	  narrows the fault to NSS, SCK or the module. Never leave this enabled
	  for a normal build — the ESC is not addressed at all.
